The Enterprise Edition is provided as is and as available. To the maximum extent the law allows, [LEGAL ENTITY NAME] disclaims every warranty, express or implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement. [LEGAL ENTITY NAME] does not warrant that the Enterprise Edition will run without interruption or without error.

A written warranty in the agreement stands. This section does not erase that warranty.

9. Liability

To the maximum extent the law allows, [LEGAL ENTITY NAME] is not liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for lost profits, lost data, or lost business, even if advised that those damages were possible.

To the maximum extent the law allows, the total liability of [LEGAL ENTITY NAME] under this license is the amount you paid for the Enterprise Edition in the 12 months before the claim. If you paid nothing, the total liability is zero.

This limit does not apply to liability that a law forbids limiting. This section does not replace a liability cap written in the agreement. The cap in the agreement applies where the agreement says it applies.

